Test suites shipped with epd-runner. These are widely redistributed chess
test positions included for engine testing only; each file is used as
distributed by its source, with the corrections noted.

bratko-kopec.epd  The Bratko-Kopec test (Danny Kopec and Ivan Bratko, 1982),
                  24 positions, ids BK.01-BK.24.
wac.epd           "Win at Chess" (Fred Reinfeld, 1945), 300 positions, the
                  corrected wacnew.epd distributed with the Arasan test set
                  (Jon Dart, https://github.com/jdart1/arasan-chess).
arasan18.epd      Arasan test suite version 18 (Jon Dart), 250 positions.
sts.epd           Strategic Test Suite (Dann Corbit and Swaminathan), themes
                  1-15 combined, graded scores in c0/c7/c8 and UCI moves in
                  c9; 1,499 positions as distributed.
eet.epd           Eigenmann Endgame Test (Walter Eigenmann), 100 positions,
                  as distributed with the Arasan test set.
quick.epd         Ten positions taken from the suites above, for smoke tests.

Results derived from these suites are stored under epd/results.
